# The planning tool's own scratch state. It writes a checkpoint after every
# tool call, so a tracked copy is a file that changes on its own and turns up
# in unrelated diffs — and what it holds is one session's position, which is
# of no use to anybody reading this repository later.
/.planning

# Analysis caches, named in phpstan.neon and rector.php so CI can restore them.
/.phpstan-cache
/.rector-cache
/coverage

# Build output from the native expansion's two test harnesses.
#
# Also declared in `native/.gitignore`, and deliberately in both. That file only
# exists on a branch that has `native/`, so on any other branch the directory is
# untracked leftover from the last build — which is exactly when a wide `git add`
# sweeps 20MB of object files into a commit. This is the copy that is always
# present.
native/.build/
native/.swiftpm/
native/android/build/
native/android/.gradle/

# Agent worktrees. Tooling that runs an agent in isolation puts a full checkout
# per agent under here, inside the repository — 693MB of other branches on the
# afternoon this was written. Untracked is not enough on its own: NativePHP's
# build rsyncs the application into the bundle and its exclude list names
# `.git`, `.github`, `.idea` and `node_modules` but not this one, so every
# worktree was being copied into the app and the copy timed out at sixty
# seconds. Ignored for the reason the block above is: what a wide `git add`
# would sweep up is the same thing a build copies.
.claude/

# What `native:install` writes. `config/nativephp.php` is the package's own
# defaults with one local line in it — the build's extra exclusions, which are
# about agent worktrees on a developer's machine and mean nothing on a clean
# checkout. `nativephp.lock` records which PHP binaries were downloaded. Both
# are regenerated by the install command and neither is a decision this
# repository makes.
config/nativephp.php
nativephp.lock

# The same command writes a CLI shim beside `artisan` so that `./native run`
# works. It is generated, it is not this repository's, and it arrives untracked
# on every machine that installs.
/native
